        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "**Yes. A component-issue event for manufacturing order `MO-25-09-1070` was created 75 minutes after the September cost period entered Pending Close. Its recorded `POSTED` status is inconsistent with Oracle’s documented treatment for newly created transactions of this type.**\n\n### Event identified\n\n| Item | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Work order number | `MO-25-09-1070` |\n| Work order ID | `WO-2025-09-004` |\n| Operation / product | Racine–Dekoven / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Source transaction | `TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070` |\n| Cost event ID | `CE-250904-0004` |\n| Event type | `INPUT` — component issue |\n| Amount | **USD $284,763.42** (`28,476,342` cents) |\n| Event date | `2025-09-30` |\n| Exact event-created time | **`2025-09-30T19:15:00`** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** |\n| Cost period | `Sep-25` / `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Recorded accounting status | **`POSTED`** |\n\n**Timing calculation:** `19:15:00 − 18:00:00 = 01:15:00`, or **75 minutes late** (4,500 seconds). Both timestamps are reproduced exactly as recorded; the source does not specify a time zone.\n\n### Policy conclusion\n\nOracle’s *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting* states that new transactions falling in or before a period in **Pending Close** will not be staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting. Transactions created after the Pending Close cutoff are held from processing until the period is closed or reopened.\n\nThe documented exceptions—revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments—do **not** cover this `INPUT`/component-issue event. Accordingly, **the recorded `POSTED` status is not consistent with the supplied Pending Close policy and timing**.\n\n**Sources:** `work_orders`, `cost_periods`, and `work_order_cost_events` in the supplied Oracle SCM source records; Oracle SCM Cost Management 26B policy excerpt, PDF page 233 / printed page 225.\n\nThe review was read-only; **no database records were changed**. The audit result and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_85c0bb4450b2/audit-report.json`.",
